<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bardi family</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bardi were a Florentine family of merchant-bankers whose company was one of the largest in 14th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, with branches from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>. With the Peruzzi they lent heavily to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-iii-of-england">Edward III of England</a> for his war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and to the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>. When Edward defaulted, the Bardi company collapsed in 1346, part of a wider Florentine banking crisis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bardi-family.jpg" alt="Bardi family" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Massimop · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coa_fam_ITA_bardi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
